The mean invalid-placement ratio decreases to zero after retiling. VQAScore and PE change only slightly, while the mean SigLIP2 score decreases. These are descriptive results for the matched subset and do not establish a general causal effect.

\subsection{Evaluation Boundaries}
PE truncates 25 of the 114 main-comparison prompts, and SigLIP2 truncates 29; the affected prompts are the same across the three systems for each metric. The evaluation uses a common yellow rendering and therefore does not assess original colors. A zero $P_{\mathrm{inv}}$ does not establish stud connectivity, physical stability, or assembly feasibility.

\section{Limitations and Discussion}
The integrated dataset count is derived from versioned release reports, and the version actually used for training needs confirmation. Dataset conversion may permit multiple grounded components, while the generation-stage single-component check has a different scope. Physical screening is based on stated assumptions and does not replace calibrated clutch-strength measurement or physical assembly tests.

The comparative evaluation covers 114 prompts and the provided outputs. The systems differ in their candidate selection and post-processing, and some text is truncated by evaluation models. These conditions limit how broadly the reported scores can be interpreted. Further paired uncertainty analysis can be conducted on the existing per-prompt records.

\section{Conclusion}
We present BrickMore, a text-to-brick framework combining LLM-assisted data construction, language-model fine-tuning, and post-generation geometric repair. The dataset workflow converts programmatically generated voxel shapes into brick layouts, while the generation pipeline predicts placements from text and checks reconstructed layouts. On 114 shared prompts, the evaluated BrickMore outputs achieve the highest means on three text--image metrics, while matching BrickGPT on mean invalid-placement ratio. The results should be interpreted under the stated evaluation and physical-screening boundaries.

